From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:01:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MLD STA: put the OCI of the receive link into an EAPOL-Key
 reply

The supplicant puts the OCI of the association link into EAPOL-Key
message 2/4 and group message 2/2, and validates message 3/4 and group
message 1/2 against that link. An AP MLD sends them on another link
where an established advertised TID-to-link mapping disables the
association link. wpa_supplicant_rx_eapol() drops the receive link that
the driver reports.

Validate the OCI of a received EAPOL-Key frame against the link that
received it, and send the reply with the OCI of that link on that link
(IEEE Std 802.11-2024 12.7.6.1 and 12.7.7.1; IEEE Std 802.11be-2024
12.2.10 names "the link used for the establishment of a security
association", and the receive link of a group message follows from
12.7.7.1). A frame with no receive link falls back to the association
link.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
